00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:37.879
- Or how you feel.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:39.839
So, Tyrese, you made a statement

00:05:40.089 --> 00:05:42.425
on draft night when you got drafted.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.552
- Yeah, I knew I wanted to do, you know

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:47.764
something. And we had such a long predraft,

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.599
and all during that predraft was,

00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:51.684
you know, the George Floyd stuff and

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.144
all these different things and

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:54.312
these different movements.

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:57.607
So, I knew that I wanted to represent my city on one side,

00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:59.400
but Black Lives Matter on the other.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.902
Like, they was talking about doing just,

00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:03.780
like, a black suit or like—I was like, "No, I need to go

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.782
to somebody who is gonna do something different."

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:06.616
- [Wade:] Yeah.

00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:07.450
- And I always knew

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:08.659
that I wanted to do a pattern of some sort.

00:06:08.659 --> 00:06:10.161
And then just putting that on the inside,

00:06:10.161 --> 00:06:11.371
I think, tied it all together.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.748
But we talked about expressing ourselves in

00:06:13.748 --> 00:06:15.625
in fashion in so many different ways.

00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:18.211
Like, I wear so many different vintage T-shirts

00:06:18.252 --> 00:06:20.838
that got like, you know, wrestling or something on it

00:06:20.838 --> 00:06:21.672
cuz that's what I like.

00:06:21.672 --> 00:06:22.507
You know what I mean?
- [Wade:] Yeah.

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:23.800
- I grew up a wrestling fan and, like, that,

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.884
like, people will know

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.886
that automatically just by seeing what I wear.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:27.720
You know what I'm saying?
- Yeah.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.806
- So, just being able to show yourself in your clothes,

00:06:29.806 --> 00:06:30.848
I think, is important.

00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:32.350
- So the confidence, just to go back to that, the confidence.

00:06:33.643 --> 00:06:36.396
The past, a lot—as athletes, you know,

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:39.315
wasn't a lot of social activism that was public.

00:06:39.649 --> 00:06:41.984
And now today it's more social activism going on.

00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:44.487
So as a young player coming in,

00:06:44.487 --> 00:06:47.573
what gave you the confidence to make

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.909
that stand or use your clothes as your voice?

00:06:50.284 --> 00:06:51.994
- Oh, just being—that's just who I am,

00:06:51.994 --> 00:06:54.580
you know? I think that's a testament to how I've been raised

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.083
and, you know, just standing up for what I believe in.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:00.169
And, you know, I think, you know,

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:02.547
the guys like you, guys like Bron, who have, you know,

00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:04.590
kinda laid that groundwork for us to,

00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:07.343
as athletes, to speak our mind and, you know,

00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:09.220
we talk about being more than an athlete and

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.847
doing all these different things.
- Yeah.

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:12.974
- You know, I think that that helps us

00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:15.059
as younger guys come into the league right away

00:07:15.059 --> 00:07:17.228
and not be afraid to use our voice and be who we are.

00:07:17.228 --> 00:07:18.062
[Upbeat guitar music]

00:07:18.062 --> 00:07:22.233
